#
# "show platform", and the per-object programming state under it.
#
# Both were commented out when vendor hardware was dropped, alongside IPMI/BMC,
# SFP, the opennsl switch plugin and the QoS hardware offload package. Those
# belong out of a software-only image. These two do not, and the name is what
# made them look alike.
#
# What "show platform dataplane" reports is which backend holds each forwarding
# object and in what state -- full, partial, no-resource, no-support,
# not-needed, error. With no offload backend loaded the answer for every object
# is the software data plane, and that is a real answer about a working system,
# not an empty one about missing hardware. It is the only operator-facing view
# of the FAL programming state there is: everything else about it is reachable
# only from vplsh, which is not a CLI and cannot be driven by the test suites.
#
# vyatta-op-show-platform-v1-yang carries the "show platform" node and its help
# text, and nothing else -- no hardware subcommands come with it. The dataplane
# package under it carries the YANG and the script it calls.
#
vyatta-op-show-platform-v1-yang
vyatta-op-show-platform-dataplane-v1-yang
